# task6_test.m8script — exercises assert_no_overlap, assert_cell_color,
# assert_row_matches, assert_slider on real screen content.
# Expected values confirmed from dump_json of actual screen output.

wait 1

# === SONG screen (default) ===

# 1. assert_no_overlap: normal rendering should have no cell written more than once
assert_no_overlap

# 2. assert_cell_color: "S" of "SONG" title, now at row 1 col 1 (the content
#    origin is (1,1) -- Renderer::setOrigin).
#    SongScreen draws the title in TEXT_TITLES. That slot is F82040, read off
#    a real M8 (hw_findings.md UI-15); it used to be written FF2040, which is
#    a colour the device cannot display -- its palette is RGB565.
assert_cell_color row 1 col 1 is F82040FF

# 3. assert_row_matches: row 3 (raw vram index, i.e. SONG row "00"'s chain-ref
#    line) should start with hex chain refs.
#    NOTE: this is the boot-loaded startup song's data (songs/neondusk.m8s as
#    of 2026-08-21; before that sunrise.m8s, and before that the in-code "Night
#    Drive" demo) -- it WILL drift again if the startup song changes. NEON DUSK
#    opens on pad and arp alone, so song row 00 rests every lane but 4 and 5.
#    Confirmed from dump_screen: " 00 -- -- -- -- 04 05 -- --"
assert_row_matches 4 "^ 00 -- -- -- -- 04 05"

# === Navigate to Instrument screen for slider test ===
key SHIFT+RIGHT
key SHIFT+RIGHT
key SHIFT+RIGHT
wait 1

# 4. assert_slider: Instrument 00's DRY slider at row 11, col 24, fill 8.
#
#    CHANGED 2026-08-19, and the old assertion was wrong rather than stale.
#    It asserted row 8 col 24 fill 8 and called that DRY, but row 8 is the
#    AMP row -- and its fill of 8 came from AMP reading the file's `volume`
#    byte (0x30 in sunrise.m8s) instead of `amp_type` (0x01). SongIO had the
#    instrument byte map shifted one field across; see AGENTS.md 7. With that
#    corrected AMP is 0x01 and its slider is empty, so keeping the old cell
#    would mean asserting fill 0 -- which cannot tell "correct" from "not
#    drawn at all".
#
#    Repointed to the slider this comment always claimed to test. DRY is 0xF0
#    on instrument 00, so the bar is full and the assertion has teeth, and
#    mixer_dry is a field whose mapping was never in doubt.
assert_slider row 12 col 25 fill 8
